\b\fs36 How to Install Resource Packs ({{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://minecraft.net/en-us/article/try-new-minecraft-java-textures" }}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf2\cf3\ul minecraft.net}}}}\f0\fs36 )\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\b0\fs28 1.\tab Locate the .zip file on your computer, for the resource pack you want to install. It\rquote ll most likely be under Downloads.\par
2.\tab Open Minecraft: Java Edition.\par
3.\tab On the main menu, select Options \f2\u10140?\f0  Resource Packs \f2\u10140?\f0  Open Resource Pack Folder.\par
4.\tab This will open your resource packs folder. From step 1, move the .zip file to this folder.\par
5.\tab Once it's done pasting, close the folder and go back to Minecraft.\par
6.\tab Reload the Resource Packs screen, by selecting Done, then Resource Packs again.\par
7.\tab Your new texture pack should now be on the available resource packs list! Select it and\'85 Done!"\par

